      "message": "chore(crypto): deprecate verifyDleqIfPresent ahead of v5 removal (#663)\n\n`verifyDleqIfPresent` will be removed in v5.0; ship the deprecation and the new\nmigration target now so consumers have a non-breaking slide before v5 ships.\n\n- `hasValidDleq` gains optional `{ require?: boolean }`. Default `true`\n  preserves the existing strict semantic (missing DLEQ on a v0/v1/v2 proof\n  returns `false`). `require: false` matches today's `verifyDleqIfPresent`\n  (missing DLEQ returns `true`, NUT-12 \"MUST verify-if-present\").\n- `verifyDleqIfPresent` is now a one-line wrapper around\n  `hasValidDleq(proof, keyset, { require: false })` and carries a\n  `@deprecated` JSDoc tag pointing at the new opt.\n\nThe default flips to `false` in v5.0 (signalled in the `hasValidDleq` JSDoc);\nthe strict policy will then be opt-in via `{ require: true }`.",
