      },
      "message": "feat: allow ProofLike in WalletEvent proof state updates (#660)\n\n`proofStateUpdates` and `proofStatesStream` only read `secret` from each\nproof to derive the subscription filter, so any `ProofLike`-shaped input\n(e.g. wallet rows loaded from storage with `amount: number` and extra\nmetadata) is accepted without first normalizing `amount` to `Amount`.\nThe original proof is echoed back on the callback/yield payload with its\ninferred input type — matching how `groupProofsByState<T extends ProofLike>`\nalready works.\n\n`proofStatesStream` also drops its `<T = unknown>` output generic in\nfavour of yielding `ProofState & { proof: P }` directly, removing the\ninternal `as unknown as T` cast and giving default-typed consumers a\nuseful payload type. Callers that previously supplied an explicit\nnon-ProofLike `<T>` (which only worked by virtue of that cast) will\nneed to drop it; runtime contract is unchanged.",
